Description:

Can you reverse a series of Linux text transformations to recover the original flag?
Start searching for the flag here nc foggy-cliff.picoctf.net 53253

Hints:
1. For text translation and character replacement, see 
trcommand documentation

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

On running the instance on the webshell we get displayed with the flag but here it is in base64 format so we had to 
run different cmds to convert this flag to its normal form:
1. base64 -d to convert it to ")p6981ppq-fa01g@ze0sfa4eG-gk3g-ta1ferirE(SGPbpvc"
2. we have to reverse the current flag using rev cmd to get the next flag as cvpbPGS(Eriref1at-g3kg-Ge4afs0ez@g10af-qpp1896p)
3. we were asked to then change the '-' to '_' using tr cmd 
4. now we were asked to convert the '()' to '{}' using the same tr cmd to get the flag as cvpbPGS{Eriref1at_g3kg_Ge4afs0ez@g10af_qpp1896p}
5. the final part was to convert this ROT13 format flag to readable form using tr 'a-zA-Z' 'n-za-mN-ZA-M' to get final flag

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solution:
picoCTF{Revers1ng_t3xt_Tr4nsf0rm@t10ns_dcc1896c}
